# Project Map

Purpose:
  Navigation map for the SDDRA project structure. Shows where human code
  and AI execution context are separated.

Structure:
  project/                 # Human code root
  .sdd/                     # AI context root
    PROJECT.sdd             # Project intent
    project/                # AI project model (schemas)
    projects/               # Concrete project instances
    chains/                 # Execution chains
    skills/                 # Reusable skills
    architecture/           # Architecture knowledge
    decisions/              # Decision ledger
    tasks/                  # Task definitions
    workflow/               # Workflow definitions
    observability/          # Observability config
    testing/                # Testing config
    security/               # Security config
    prompts/                # Prompt templates
    plugins/                # Plugin adapters
    patterns/               # Reusable patterns
    runtime/                # Runtime state
    context/                # Context routing
    dependencies/           # Dependency rules
    gates/                  # Quality gates
    stages/                 # Stage definitions
    standards/              # Coding standards
    state/                  # State management
    templates/              # Document templates
    workflow/               # Workflow engine
    workflows/              # Workflow definitions

Separation:
  Human code lives in project/
  AI context lives in .sdd/
  Concrete project instances live in .sdd/projects/<name>/

Rules:
  [MAP1] Human code and AI context MUST be separated.
  [MAP2] Concrete project data MUST NOT live in .sdd/project/.
  [MAP3] .sdd/projects/<name>/ is the only location for concrete project instances.

State: +